    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Pricing &amp; billing</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Is there really no design deposit? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, really. Traditional agencies charge somewhere between three and five thousand dollars up front, and I charge nothing. Your first $175 payment is what kicks off the build, and that is the entire intake fee.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What does the $175/month actually cover? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The flat monthly rate covers custom design, the custom-coded build of up to ten pages, hosting, SSL, unlimited content updates, direct support from me, mobile-first responsive design, the on-page and local SEO foundation, and ongoing security monitoring. All of that comes in for one price.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why a 12-month minimum on the monthly plan? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The reason is that I do the full custom build with nothing down on your end, and the twelve-month commitment is how the math comes out even on mine. After the first year is behind you, the arrangement becomes month-to-month with thirty days of notice required to cancel.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I need to cancel early? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The remaining monthly payments are due per the service agreement. I do not love early-cancel situations, so I usually find a way to work it out, but the written agreement is what governs.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I buy out the monthly plan to own the code? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. If you decide later that you would rather own the code outright, I will quote a buyout. Ask any time; it is a straightforward conversation.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What's the lump-sum option? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The lump-sum option is $4,000 one-time for a custom-coded site of up to ten pages, with code ownership transferred to you on delivery. Hosting is optional at $50 a month, and any updates after launch are billed hourly at $150 an hour. It tends to suit businesses that want to pay once and then handle the site themselves.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">The website</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How long does it take to build my site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Most sites are designed, built, and launched within two to three weeks of the discovery call. The timing depends mostly on how quickly you send me content from your side, namely the logo, photos, and service details.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How many pages do I get? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Both plans include up to ten content pages, and extra pages beyond that (whether additional services, additional locations, or other new content pages) are $150 each. Most service businesses are well covered by six to eight pages, namely home, about, services, service area, FAQ, and contact.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do I own my website? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">With the monthly plan, I own and host the code; that is how I can build a custom site with $0 down. With the lump-sum option, you own the code on delivery.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I update the site myself? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You do not need to update the site yourself, since unlimited updates are part of the plan. You email or text me with what you want changed, and the change tends to land quickly on most business days. If you do want a simple CMS for blogging on top of that, I can add one.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What about my existing site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I coordinate the launch so there is no downtime. Once the new site is live, you can take the old one offline or archive it; your call.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I have a blog? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. A blog section is a $200 one-time add-on; includes the blog index, a post template, and an RSS feed. After that, new posts are part of your unlimited updates.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Process &amp; support</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What's the discovery call like? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">About 20&ndash;30 minutes on Google Meet (or the phone if you prefer). I learn about your business, your customers, and your goals for the site. I answer your questions. If I am the right fit, I send a simple service agreement and I get started.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Who am I actually working with? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Jon Ajinga, founder, based in Colorado Springs. No account managers, no offshore developers, no handoffs. The person writing your code is the person you email. See <a href="/about/" class="inline-link">the about page</a>.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I don't have a logo or photos? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No problem. I can design a simple logo (from $300) or help you find a local photographer. I can also work with what you have and fill in gaps with carefully chosen stock imagery.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How fast is support? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Routine content updates tend to land quickly on most business days. Emergencies, meaning the site being down, wrong information being live, or an urgent correction, jump the queue and get handled fast. Email, phone, or text all reach me directly, and I am available for quick turnarounds on most business days.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you work with businesses outside Colorado? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. I am fully remote and work with small businesses across the U.S. and Canada. Distance does not change the work or the price.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">SEO &amp; performance</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you guarantee Google rankings? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Nobody can; if they do, be skeptical. What we guarantee: a fast, accessible, well-structured site with clean on-page SEO, local business schema, proper sitemaps, and strong Core Web Vitals. That's the foundation. Rankings come from that plus time, content, and reviews.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What PageSpeed score should I expect? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Every site I build runs at 95 to 100 on Google PageSpeed Insights, both mobile and desktop, and load times tend to come in under one second.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will my site be accessible? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. I build to WCAG 2.2 AA as the baseline, with real contrast, real focus states, and real keyboard navigation. None of it is a plugin we switch on after the fact.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will I get Google Analytics? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I set up privacy-focused analytics by default using <span class="term" data-term="A lightweight, cookie-free analytics tool that respects privacy and doesn't require a cookie banner.">Umami</span> and <span class="term" data-term="Cloudflare's free server-side analytics that never leaves your visitors' browsers.">Cloudflare Web Analytics</span>; both fast, both cookie-banner-free. If you'd prefer Google Analytics 4, I can add it at no cost.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Forms &amp; operational pages</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What forms does my site come with? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">At minimum, a contact form powered by <span class="term" data-term="A lightweight third-party form backend that handles submissions without needing a server. Fast, spam-resistant, cookie-free.">Web3Forms</span> plus a matching thank-you page that appears after submission. Beyond that, I can add industry-specific forms; emergency service requests for HVAC and plumbing, free-inspection requests for roofing, bid forms for contractors, schedule-an-inspection forms for home inspectors, and so on. See the <a href="/sample-forms/" class="inline-link">sample forms gallery</a> for eight industry examples.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What are "operational pages" and do they count against my page limit? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Operational pages are the infrastructure pages every professional site needs: Privacy Policy, Accessibility Statement, Terms of Use, Contact, Thank-You, Style Guide, and Sitemap. They don't count against your 10 content pages. Every build includes all seven as standard; you're covered legally, ethically, and technically from day one.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What technical files come with the site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You won't see them, but they're there: <code>robots.txt</code> (tells search engines what to crawl), <code>humans.txt</code> (credits the build team), <code>sitemap.xml</code> (submitted to Google for you), <code>security.txt</code> (how to report security issues), a branded <code>404</code> page, a full favicon suite, and Open Graph / Twitter images for when your links are shared. All set up once, at build time, no maintenance.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How do I request a content change once the site is live? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The fastest way is the <a href="/content-update/" class="inline-link">content update form</a> in your client portal; it lands in my inbox structured and ready to act on. Email at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.email }}</a> or phone/text at <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a> also work. All three go to the same place.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if the site is down and I need help right now? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Call or text me first at <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>, and then, if you can, fill out the <a href="/emergency/" class="inline-link">emergency support form</a> with the details, including what is happening, when it started, and any error messages on the screen. Emergencies skip the queue, and I am available for quick turnarounds on most business days.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I give feedback on the design while you're building? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Please do; that's the whole point of the preview link. The <a href="/design-feedback/" class="inline-link">design feedback form</a> is structured so every note lands in one place. Unlimited rounds, no charge per change. I would rather get it right than fast.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you pay referral fees? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, modestly. If you refer a business and they become a client, we credit one month of hosting to your account (or send a simple cash thank-you if you're not a client). Use the <a href="/refer/" class="inline-link">referral form</a>; it takes about a minute.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Demos &amp; samples</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">The demo sites look really different from each other. Will my site be locked into one of those styles? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. The six <a href="/samples/" class="inline-link">demo sites</a> exist to show that I tune the design to each industry, not the other way around. Your site will look like your business, not like a template. The demos are reference points for visual voice; your build is its own thing.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Are the demos real working sites? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Every link, form, mobile menu, and theme toggle works. Submit a sample form and you'll get a real "thank you" page; no submission is sent because the access keys are sandboxed. They're functional builds, not screenshots.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why are sample form intakes so detailed? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Because real intakes are. Our <a href="/sample-forms/" class="inline-link">sample forms</a> show what a contractor actually needs to triage a job: scope, urgency, address, photos, access. A "name + email + message" form converts higher; an industry-specific intake gives you a usable lead. I default to the second.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I see one of your real client builds? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">After I have launched a few I will add a portfolio. For now the <a href="/samples/" class="inline-link">demos</a> represent our standard for quality, layout, and engineering. The site you're reading is also fully representative of what I ship.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Onboarding &amp; client portal</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What does onboarding actually involve? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">After the discovery call I send you to the <a href="/onboarding/" class="inline-link">onboarding form</a>. It's nine sections covering your business, services, customers, brand, current site, Google profile, credentials, and any specific deadlines. Most clients fill it out in 15 to 25 minutes. You can save what you have and come back; nothing has to be done in one sitting.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do I have to use the onboarding form? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. If you'd rather send me a Google Doc, a Dropbox Paper file, a Notion page, or a stack of emails, that works. The form just gives structure so I do not miss anything obvious. Same outcome either way.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What's in the client portal? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The <a href="/client-portal/" class="inline-link">client portal</a> is one bookmarkable page with everything an existing client needs: onboarding (if you're new), design feedback (if you're in build), content updates and emergency support (if you're live), plus referrals, testimonials, and resource links. Four stages. Pick the one you're in.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Is there a login? Will I have a dashboard? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No login. No dashboard. I deliberately don't build admin panels because they're a maintenance burden and a security target you don't need. Everything you'd do in a dashboard (request a change, see your form submissions, download an invoice) is one email or one form away.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Domain, email, and ownership</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Who owns my domain? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You do. I do not register domains on a client's behalf because it creates the wrong control structure on the wrong day. Your domain stays at your registrar in your name; I just point its DNS at my hosting. If you've lost track of where it lives, I will help you find it.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you handle email on my domain? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I do not host email, but I set up the DNS records (MX, SPF, DKIM, DMARC) for whichever provider you choose: Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, or simple forwarding. I never charge for the configuration; it's part of launch.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What happens to my domain if I lose track of the renewal? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I monitor WHOIS expiration directly, not via the registrar's email (which often gets lost). I send reminders at 60, 30, and 7 days before expiration so it never lapses. If it does lapse, most TLDs have a 30-day redemption window; I can help recover it.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">If I cancel, can I take my site elsewhere? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. On the lump-sum plan you already own the code; we transfer the GitHub repo. On the monthly plan I will provide a static export of the live site (clean HTML/CSS/JS) that runs on any host with no dependencies. Your domain, your content, your forms account: all yours. No exit fee.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Privacy &amp; data</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will my site need a cookie banner? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. The default stack (Bunny Fonts, Cloudflare Web Analytics, Umami) is fully cookie-free and GDPR-compliant by design. I only add a cookie banner if you specifically opt into a tracker that requires one (Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, etc.). I discourage that path; it slows the site and gets blocked anyway.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Where do form submissions go? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Straight to your business email via <span class="term" data-term="A lightweight third-party form backend that handles submissions without needing a server.">Web3Forms</span>. There's no copy stored on our side. I never see your messages unless you forward one to us.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you sell data, share with ad networks, or use trackers? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No, no, and no. Read the <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="inline-link">privacy policy</a>. The whole stack is built around not collecting personal data I do not need.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Maintenance &amp; the long term</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How do I know if something I'm asking for is "an update" vs. "a new feature"? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Editing existing pages (text, images, hours, prices, photos, seasonal callouts) is a content update; included on the monthly plan, no extra charge. Adding a new page (an extra service page, a new location, a new resource) is a new page; $150 each, billed once. Adding a new behavior (calculator, gallery, video player, e-commerce) is a feature; I quote it before starting. I always tell you in advance whether a request is included or billable.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What happens during a Cloudflare outage? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Most Cloudflare incidents affect a region, not the global network, so visitors in other regions still see your site. If the outage is global, your site is unreachable for the duration; I monitor Cloudflare's status feed and post updates. In twelve months of running this stack I have had one global incident, lasted 27 minutes, affected ~4% of global traffic.</div></div>
